As an upcoming designer, I believe spacecraft design represents one of the most exciting opportunities to explore the relationship between imagination, technology, engineering, and art. Unlike conventional vehicles, spacecraft are designed to operate beyond Earth's atmosphere, where traditional design limitations no longer apply in the same way.
A spacecraft is more than a machine built for space travel. It is a combination of functionality, structural innovation, human experience, and futuristic aesthetics. Every curve, surface, component, and proportion contributes to its identity and purpose.
